Move scope-level rule-body checks to the Rust side

Add a new `scope_checks` pass that runs after `resolve_scopes` and
catches the three compile errors that need name resolution but not
type inference:

- VariableIntroducedInThenStmt
- ThenDefinedVarNotNew
- MatchPatternArgVarIsNotFresh

The pass collects findings into a `Vec<CompileError>` which is chained
into `check_eqlog`'s `.min()`, so the existing error-priority ordering
still applies when both scope and eqlog-side errors are present in the
same theory.

Remove the corresponding iterators from `semantics::check_epic` and
`semantics` so these errors now have a single source. The eqlog-side
rules that populate the related predicates still run but their outputs
are no longer consumed; cleaning up `eqlog.eql` is left for a follow-up.
